  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a poster, I want to add a photo from my library or camera, so that it is uploaded and inserted as BBCode.\n\n### Scope\n\nPhoto picker and camera, downscale per setting, upload through LOT-056 after notice N1 (first use, per device), insert per BBCode mode/size variant. Settings kept with legacy keys.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: LOT-071 T4 and notice N1\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `AnswerView.swift` (`ReplyImageInsertionView`, `ReplyPhotoLibraryPicker`, `ReplyUIKitImagePicker`), `ReplyService.swift` (`Img3ReplyImageUploadService`, `RehostPreferences`, `RehostBBCodeMode`, `RehostUploadMaxDimension`, `RehostImageSizeVariant`)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-102-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-056 (#82, ready)\n- LOT-084 (#176)\n- LOT-060 (#85, done)\n- LOT-160 (#250)\n\n### Blocked by\n\ndependencies not done: LOT-056 (#82, ready), LOT-084 (#176), LOT-160 (#250)\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- #134\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No upload before N1 is accepted; refusal sends nothing.\n- [ ] Whether EXIF/GPS is stripped is measured on the Mac and stated in the spec (audit D §10 Q9).\n- [ ] Upload failures keep the composer text and show the host's error.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
